<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!-- LibSmb: an SMB 2/3 file server in plain C#, from Microsoft's open specification [MS-SMB2]: dialects 2.0.2 to 3.0.2,
       NTLMv2 through SPNEGO or guests, signing, compounding, Apple's extensions for macOS. It serves any ISmbFileSystem;
       LocalFileSystem serves a folder. Nothing of AnyFS's, and no dependency but Microsoft's logging abstractions. It is
       its own package on NuGet.org, with its own version (below, not AnyFS's): a tag libsmb-v<Version> publishes it
       (.github/workflows/libsmb.yml). -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AssemblyName>LibSmb</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>LibSmb</RootNamespace>
    <Version>0.2.0</Version>
    <!-- what changed in this version, as NuGet.org shows it: rewritten with each version -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.2.0
- A connection's requests run side by side, so a slow file system call holds up only its own request (MaxConcurrentRequests, 64 by default). An ISmbFileSystem is therefore called from several requests at once; one open's calls still never overlap, and its READs and WRITEs keep the order they were sent in.
- A request that takes long gets an interim STATUS_PENDING reply (InterimResponseDelay, half a second by default), so clients wait it out; a client's CANCEL fires the call's cancellation token.
- A file system call that gives up with an OperationCanceledException fails its own command with STATUS_IO_TIMEOUT, also inside a compound chain, and the connection carries on. A CLOSE closes its file whatever becomes of the request.
- READs and WRITEs carry 64 KiB. The megabyte offered before stalled a Mac's writes and could hang it.
- A port a server listens on is its own. On Linux and macOS a second server on it started without an error and took connections; it is refused now.
- A session's messages are signed on several processors at once.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Product>LibSmb</Product>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>LibSmb</PackageId>
    <Title>LibSmb</Title>
    <Description>An SMB 2/3 file server in pure C# (dialects 2.0.2 to 3.0.2, NTLMv2 or guest, signing, compounding, Apple's macOS extensions) that serves shares from any file system you implement, or a local folder. No admin rights: listen on any port.</Description>
    <PackageTags>smb;smb2;smb3;cifs;file-server;file-sharing;ntlm</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/fiddyschmitt/AnyFS/tree/main/src/LibSmb</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="LibSmb.Tests" />
    <!-- AnyFS's SMB mount tests use LibSmb.Tests' client (linked), which reads the wire with these internals -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="AnyFS.Mounts.Tests" />
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
